Inclusion Criteria:

Patients must meet all of the following inclusion criteria to be eligible for inclusion in the study:

1. Patients with at least 1 inpatient or 2 outpatient diagnoses (30 days apart) with ICD-10-CM code for ATTRwt-CM (E85.82), ATTRv-CM (E85.0, E85.2), or organ-limited amyloidosis (E85.4) and with ≥ 1 dispensed fill of tafamidis; OR For those who do not meet the ATTR-CM diagnosis criterion, patients with ≥ 1 dispensed fill of tafamidis;
2. Age ≥ 18 years on the index date;
3. With ≥ 6 months' activity before the index date.

Exclusion Criteria

Patients meeting any of the following criteria will not be included in the study:

1. ≥1 ICD-10-CM diagnosis code for light chain amyloidosis (E85.81) during the study period;
2. ≥ 1 ICD-10-CM diagnosis code for ATTR-PN (E85.1) or prescription fill for patisiran or eplontersen during the study period;
3. ≥1 ICD-10-CM for liver or heart transplant during the baseline period (ICD codes included in the SAP);
4. ≥1 ICD-10-CM code for multiple myeloma during the baseline period (ICD codes included in the SAP);
5. Dispensed fill for any of the following DMTs during baseline period: tafamidis, acoramidis, vutrisiran (codes included in the SAP);
6. Dispensed fill for any of the following therapies during the study period (for excluding patients with amyloid light-chain amyloidosis): melphalan, cyclophosphamide, bortezomib, lenalidomide, thalidomide, bendamustine, pomalidomide, carfilzomib, ixazomib, daratumumab, venetoclax, elotuzumab, ibrutinib, rituximab and obinutuzumab (codes included in the SAP).
